            }
          ],
          "text": "Instructions for use"
        },
        "language": "en",
        "subject": [
          {
            "reference": "MedicinalProductDefinition/sakura-bloom-20mg"
          }
        ],
        "date": "2026-11-02",
        "author": [
          {
            "reference": "Organization/sakura-pharma-eu"
          }
        ],
        "title": "Sakura Bloom 20 mg film-coated tablets - Instructions for use",
        "section": [
          {
            "id": "i-ifu-0",
            "title": "Instructions for use",
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "system": "http://example.org/fhir-gra/CodeSystem/ifu-section",
                  "code": "ifu-0",
                  "display": "INSTRUCTIONS FOR USE"
                }
              ],
              "text": "INSTRUCTIONS FOR USE"
            },
            "text": {
              "status": "additional",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p><i>Synthetic example. Sakura Bloom and Sakuramil are fictitious. This text was written for a FHIR ePI demonstration and must not be used for any clinical purpose.</i></p><p><b>Sakura Bloom 20 mg film-coated tablets</b><br/>Opening the bottle and taking your tablet</p><p>For the 30-tablet bottle with a child-resistant cap. Read these steps the first time you open a new bottle.</p><p><b>You will need:</b> the bottle and a glass of water.</p></div>"
            },
            "section": [
              {
                "id": "i-ifu-1",
                "title": "Step 1. Check the pack",
                "code": {
                  "coding": [
                    {
                      "system": "http://example.org/fhir-gra/CodeSystem/ifu-section",
                      "code": "ifu-1",
                      "display": "Step 1. Check the pack"
                    }
                  ],
                  "text": "Step 1. Check the pack"
                },
                "text": {
                  "status": "additional",
                  "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p><img src=\"#picto-1\" alt=\"Step 1 pictogram\"/></p><p>Check the expiry date on the label and that the cap has not been opened.</p></div>"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "i-ifu-2",
                "title": "Step 2. Push down and turn",
                "code": {
                  "coding": [
                    {
                      "system": "http://example.org/fhir-gra/CodeSystem/ifu-section",
                      "code": "ifu-2",
                      "display": "Step 2. Push down and turn"
                    }
                  ],
                  "text": "Step 2. Push down and turn"
                },
                "text": {
                  "status": "additional",
                  "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p><img src=\"#picto-2\" alt=\"Step 2 pictogram\"/></p><p>Press the cap down firmly and, while pressing, turn it anticlockwise to open.</p></div>"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "i-ifu-3",
                "title": "Step 3. Remove the seal",
                "code": {
                  "coding": [
                    {
                      "system": "http://example.org/fhir-gra/CodeSystem/ifu-section",
                      "code": "ifu-3",
                      "display": "Step 3. Remove the seal"
                    }
                  ],
                  "text": "Step 3. Remove the seal"
                },
                "text": {
                  "status": "additional",
                  "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p><img src=\"#picto-3\" alt=\"Step 3 pictogram\"/></p><p>The first time only, peel off the foil seal using the tab. Do not use the bottle if the seal is broken.</p></div>"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "i-ifu-4",
                "title": "Step 4. Take out one tablet",
                "code": {
                  "coding": [
                    {
                      "system": "http://example.org/fhir-gra/CodeSystem/ifu-section",
                      "code": "ifu-4",
                      "display": "Step 4. Take out one tablet"
                    }
                  ],
                  "text": "Step 4. Take out one tablet"
                },
                "text": {
                  "status": "additional",
                  "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p><img src=\"#picto-4\" alt=\"Step 4 pictogram\"/></p><p>Tip one tablet into your hand. Check it is pale red, round and marked SB.</p></div>"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "i-ifu-5",
                "title": "Step 5. Swallow it whole",
                "code": {
                  "coding": [
                    {
                      "system": "http://example.org/fhir-gra/CodeSystem/ifu-section",
                      "code": "ifu-5",
                      "display": "Step 5. Swallow it whole"
                    }
                  ],
                  "text": "Step 5. Swallow it whole"
                },
                "text": {
                  "status": "additional",
                  "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p><img src=\"#picto-5\" alt=\"Step 5 pictogram\"/></p><p>Swallow the tablet whole with a glass of water, with or without food. Do not crush or chew it.</p></div>"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "i-ifu-6",
                "title": "Step 6. Close the cap",
                "code": {
                  "coding": [
                    {
                      "system": "http://example.org/fhir-gra/CodeSystem/ifu-section",
                      "code": "ifu-6",
                      "display": "Step 6. Close the cap"
                    }
                  ],
                  "text": "Step 6. Close the cap"
                },
                "text": {
                  "status": "additional",
                  "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p><img src=\"#picto-6\" alt=\"Step 6 pictogram\"/></p><p>Turn the cap clockwise until it clicks, so children cannot open it. Keep the bottle out of the sight and reach of children.</p></div>"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "i-ifu-7",
                "title": "If you have trouble opening the cap",
                "code": {
                  "coding": [
                    {
                      "system": "http://example.org/fhir-gra/CodeSystem/ifu-section",
                      "code": "ifu-7",
                      "display": "If you have trouble opening the cap"
                    }
                  ],
                  "text": "If you have trouble opening the cap"
                },
                "text": {
                  "status": "additional",
                  "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p>Ask your pharmacist about other ways to open it. Do not move the tablets to another container. For dosing, missed doses and side effects, read the package leaflet.</p></div>"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
